<<<
The first is usually pronounced with soft g, & occasionally spelt ji- ; the second is pronounced with hard g, & was sometimes spelt gui- or ghi- to mark the fact.
===
The first is usually pronounced with soft g, & occasionally spelt *ji-*; the second is pronounced with hard g, & was sometimes spelt gui- or ghi- to mark the fact.
>>>

<<<
It is doubtful whether one is derived from the other. For gibberish, lingo, &c., see JARGON.
===
It is doubtful whether one is derived from the other. For *gibberish, lingo,* &c., see ^^JARGON^^.
>>>

